course: dictionary
lesson: 2725
title: Dioxide: two oxygens and a partner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dioxide is a chemical substance whose molecules have two oxygen atoms joined to another atom. Look at the word parts: di means two, and oxide means a substance with oxygen in it.
explain: In everyday talk, dioxide almost always means carbon dioxide, written CO₂. «Breathed-out air contains less oxygen and more carbon dioxide than breathed-in air.» The sentence tells you that carbon dioxide is something we breathe out.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» Carbon dioxide is a gas, so the air is the right place for it. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Dioxide means a substance with two oxygen atoms joined to another atom.
fact: In everyday use, dioxide almost always means carbon dioxide (CO₂).
fact: Carbon dioxide is a colourless gas that we breathe out.
fact: Plants take in carbon dioxide to make food, in a process called photosynthesis.
fact: Too much carbon dioxide in the air traps heat and warms the Earth.
exercise: What does the di- in dioxide mean? | Carbon | Three | *Two | Half
exercise: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» What is being added to the air? | Heat from the sun | Nitrogen | Oxygen | *Carbon dioxide
exercise: Which gas do plants take in to make food? | Titanium dioxide | Oxygen | *Carbon dioxide | Nitrogen
test: «Carbon dioxide traps heat like a blanket.» What does this comparison suggest? | Blankets are made of carbon dioxide | *Carbon dioxide keeps heat in, like a blanket keeps warmth in | Carbon dioxide is a solid | Carbon dioxide cools the planet down
test: Which of these is a dioxide that comes from volcanoes and pollution? | Oxygen | Carbon monoxide | Titanium dioxide | *Sulphur dioxide
exam: According to «carbon dioxide, a waste gas, passes out to be breathed away», what is carbon dioxide? | A type of lung | *A waste gas that leaves the body when we breathe out | A tube that carries air to the lungs | Oxygen that goes into the blood
